1. Definitions

For the purposes of this License:

“Original Repository” means the source repository available at:

https://github.com/Cesarcfw/portifolio

“Licensed Material” means the source code, project structure,
configuration files and original technical documentation contained in
the Original Repository and created by the Copyright Holder.

“Personal Content” means the Copyright Holder’s personal information,
name beyond the attribution required by this License, photographs,
profile images, biography, curriculum vitae, professional history,
contact information, project descriptions, testimonials, personal
branding, logos and other content that identifies or represents the
Copyright Holder.

“Derived Portfolio” means a website, application or repository that
reuses or adapts a substantial portion of the Licensed Material,
including its source code, components, project structure, architecture
or layout organization.

2. Grant of Permission

Subject to the conditions of this License, permission is granted, free
of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of the Licensed Material to:

a. use the Licensed Material for personal, educational or professional
portfolio projects;

b. copy, modify, adapt and reorganize the Licensed Material;

c. publish and host a Derived Portfolio;

d. distribute modified versions of the Licensed Material;

e. use the Licensed Material to create a customized portfolio for a
specific client;

f. use a Derived Portfolio to present professional experience, skills,
projects and services.

3. Required Attribution

Every publicly available Derived Portfolio must provide clear
attribution to the Original Repository.

The attribution must be included in at least one of the following
locations:

a. the README file of the Derived Portfolio repository;

b. an “About”, “Credits”, “Acknowledgements” or similarly named section
of the published portfolio;

c. another reasonably visible location associated with the Derived
Portfolio.

The attribution must include:

a. the name “César Maluf”; and

b. a functional link to:

https://github.com/Cesarcfw/portifolio

The following wording may be used:

“Portfolio structure inspired by the project created by César Maluf:
https://github.com/Cesarcfw/portifolio”

Equivalent wording is permitted provided that the original source and
author remain clear.

Attribution must not be hidden, removed through styling, placed only in
source code comments or made practically inaccessible to ordinary
users or repository visitors.

4. Personal Content Is Excluded

This License does not grant permission to copy, publish, redistribute
or reuse Personal Content.

Any person using the Licensed Material must replace the Copyright
Holder’s Personal Content with their own information before publicly
publishing a Derived Portfolio.

In particular, users must not reuse the Copyright Holder’s:

a. biography;

b. curriculum vitae;

c. employment history;

d. contact information;

e. photographs;

f. testimonials or recommendations;

g. personal project descriptions;

h. credentials, tokens or configuration secrets;

i. personal branding or visual identity elements that could reasonably
cause confusion regarding authorship or identity.

5. No False Authorship

A Derived Portfolio may identify its developer as the author of their
own modifications, customization and personal content.

However, no person may:

a. claim to be the sole or original author of the Original Repository;

b. remove the attribution required by this License;

c. represent the Original Repository as having been created entirely
by another person;

d. use the Copyright Holder’s name, image or identity in a manner that
suggests ownership, partnership, sponsorship or endorsement.

6. Commercial and Professional Use

A Derived Portfolio may be used for professional and commercial
purposes, including:

a. advertising professional services;

b. obtaining employment or freelance work;

c. developing a customized portfolio for a specific client;

d. charging a client for customization, implementation, deployment or
support services.

However, the Licensed Material may not be sold, sublicensed or
redistributed substantially unchanged as:

a. a generic portfolio template;

b. a boilerplate package;

c. a downloadable commercial product;

d. course material;

e. a template marketplace product;

f. a collection or bundle of templates;

without prior written authorization from the Copyright Holder.

A project is considered “substantially unchanged” when its primary
value continues to come from the Original Repository and only minor
changes have been made to text, colors, images, branding or
configuration.

7. Modification and Distribution

Modified versions of the Licensed Material may be distributed,
provided that:

a. the required attribution is preserved;

b. this License or a copy of its attribution and Personal Content
conditions accompanies the distributed Licensed Material;

c. modifications are not represented as part of the Original Repository
unless they were accepted into it by the Copyright Holder;

d. third-party license notices are preserved when required.

A Derived Portfolio may use another license for original modifications
created by its developer, but the attribution, Personal Content and
false-authorship conditions of this License must continue to apply to
the portions derived from the Original Repository.

